.TH SDL_GetAudioDeviceGain 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetAudioDeviceGain \- Get the gain of an audio device.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_audio.h>
.PP
.BI "float SDL_GetAudioDeviceGain(SDL_AudioDeviceID devid);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The gain of a device is its volume; a larger gain means a louder output, with a gain of zero being silence\[char46]
.PP
Audio devices default to a gain of 1\[char46]0f (no change in output)\[char46]
.PP
Physical devices may not have their gain changed, only logical devices, and this function will always return -1\[char46]0f when used on physical devices\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I devid
the audio device to query\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the gain of the device or -1\[char46]0f on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_SetAudioDeviceGain (3)
